#!/bin/zsh
#
# voiced：构建、启动、停止、重启 voiced 服务和 Voiced 应用。
# 在仓库根目录直接运行 ./voiced，或用 ./install.sh 安装为系统命令 voiced（./uninstall.sh 删除）。
#
#   voiced                       显示帮助（同 voiced help）
#   voiced <部分> [操作]         部分：service、macos、ios、core；不给操作时用上下箭头选择
#   voiced <操作> [部分]         操作：build、start、stop、restart；不给部分时用上下箭头选择
#   voiced status                显示服务和 Mac 版的状态
#
# 例：voiced service restart、voiced restart ios、voiced build core、voiced ios deploy。
# restart 总是先 git pull（只快进）再构建。服务（service/，Rust）由 launchd 运行；core/VoicedCore 是两个应用共用的 Swift 库。
# 每句话如何处理（输入、输入后回车、用 Claude Code 执行）由 iPhone 上的“发送到 Mac”方式决定，
# Claude Code 的文件夹也在 iPhone 上设置。

set -euo pipefail

# :A resolves the /usr/local/bin/voiced symlink, so paths point into the checkout.
ROOT="${0:A:h}"
SERVICE="$ROOT/service"
CORE="$ROOT/core/VoicedCore"

LABEL="com.local.voiced.input"
DOMAIN="gui/$(id -u)"
SERVICE_EXECUTABLE="$SERVICE/.build/voiced"
PLIST="$HOME/Library/LaunchAgents/$LABEL.plist"
LOG="$HOME/Library/Logs/VoicedInput.log"

UI_APP="$ROOT/macos/.build/Voiced.app"
UI_EXECUTABLE="$UI_APP/Contents/MacOS/Voiced"

IOS_BUNDLE_ID="com.voiced.personal.ios"

usage() {
    print -u2 "Usage: voiced service [build|start|stop|restart|status]"
    print -u2 "       voiced macos [build|start|stop|restart]"
    print -u2 "       voiced ios [build [device]|start [device]|stop|restart [device]|deploy [device]]"
    print -u2 "       voiced core [build]"
    print -u2 "       voiced build [all|core|service|ios|macos] [device]"
    print -u2 "       voiced restart [all|service|ios|macos] [device]"
    print -u2 "       voiced start [all|service|macos|ios]"
    print -u2 "       voiced stop [all|service|macos|ios]"
    print -u2 "       voiced status"
    print -u2 "       voiced help"
    exit 2
}

show_help() {
    cat <<'HELP'
voiced builds and runs the parts of Voiced: the voiced service, which types what Voiced on the
iPhone hears at the Mac's cursor (service/, Rust), the Mac app (macos/), the iOS app (ios/) and
the library both apps share (core/VoicedCore).

  voiced service start         start the service, and at every login

Name a part, then what to do with it; leave out what to do to pick it with the arrow keys:

  voiced service [build|start|stop|restart|status]
                               start: also at every login; stop: no longer at login
  voiced macos [build|start|stop|restart]
  voiced ios [build|start|stop|restart|deploy]
                               build: for the simulator (build device: for an iPhone)
                               start, restart: pick a connected iPhone or a simulator, then build,
                               install and open the app there (… device: the paired iPhone, no list)
                               stop: quit the app on the iPhone or simulator you pick
                               deploy [name]: build, install and open on the paired iPhone, or the
                               one named
  voiced core [build]          build the shared library on its own

Or name what to do, then the part; leave out the part to pick it with the arrow keys:

  voiced build [all|core|service|ios|macos] [device]
                               all: the service and both apps (they build core themselves);
                               device: build iOS for an iPhone rather than the simulator
  voiced restart [all|service|ios|macos] [device]
                               always pulls (fast-forward only) and builds first; all: the
                               service and the Mac app, then the app on the paired iPhone
  voiced start [all|service|macos|ios]
                               all: the service and the Mac app, then the app on the paired iPhone
  voiced stop [all|service|macos|ios]
                               all: the service, the Mac app, and the app on every connected
                               iPhone and booted simulator

  voiced status                show the service and the Mac app
  voiced help                  show this

What happens to each sentence (typed at the cursor, typed and followed by Return, or run
by Claude Code) is the "Send to Mac" mode chosen on the iPhone, as is the folder Claude Code
runs in.
